      <title>PANDORA: Jailbreak GPTs by Retrieval Augmented Generation Poisoning</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/publication/pandora/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 01 Feb 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/publication/pandora/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Distinguished Paper Award&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;PANDORA introduces a novel attack vector against RAG-enhanced LLM systems. By strategically poisoning retrieval databases, attackers can effectively bypass safety mechanisms in models like GPT-4, highlighting critical security considerations for RAG deployments.&lt;/p&gt;
